SET_NETDEV_DEV must point at the GMAC platform device, not the MDIO bus
parent. The slowpath datapath DMA-maps against netdev->dev.parent; on
boards where the PHYs sit on a bitbanged mdio-gpio bus that parent has no
dma_mask, dma_map_page_attrs() fails (WARN at kernel/dma/mapping.c) and
the GMAC DMA engine is given an invalid address — the SoC hard-resets on
the first frames. Same fix as the 23.05-era MR52 patch 0110; the old code
even carried a "(netdev, &pdev->dev) ?" comment suspecting this.

--- a/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
+++ b/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
@@ -1432,8 +1432,15 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* workaround for tplink,onhub eth0 phy_attach_direct panic with poll enabled */
-	SET_NETDEV_DEV(netdev, gmacdev->miibus->parent); /* (netdev, &pdev->dev) ? */
+	/*
+	 * Bind the netdev to the GMAC platform device, not the MDIO bus
+	 * parent: phy_attach_direct() needs a non-NULL parent, and the
+	 * slowpath DMA maps pages against this device — the mdio bus parent
+	 * (bitbanged mdio-gpio on MR52) has no dma_mask, so mappings fail
+	 * and the GMAC DMA engine gets fed an invalid address, hard-resetting
+	 * the SoC on first traffic.
+	 */
+	SET_NETDEV_DEV(netdev, &pdev->dev);
 
 	/*
 	 * Connect PHY
